# Project Architecture

Municipal Property Tax Survey Management System — **pnpm + Turborepo** monorepo.

## Apps

| App           | Tech                                                 | Port | Responsibility                                           |
| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ---- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| `apps/web`    | Next.js 16, React 19, Clerk, TanStack Query          | 3000 | Admin dashboard UI                                       |
| `apps/api`    | NestJS 11, Clerk JWT, BullMQ producers               | 4000 | HTTP API, business logic, auth, data access              |
| `apps/worker` | NestJS 11, BullMQ consumers, Playwright PDF          | 4001 | Background jobs (ETL, imports, exports, storage cleanup) |
| `apps/mobile` | Expo SDK 57, RN 0.86, Expo Router, `@expo/ui`, Clerk | —    | Field/surveyor mobile client                             |

## Packages

| Package                        | Purpose                                                    |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| `@workspace/database`          | Prisma 7 client, generated types, enums, RBAC/seed helpers |
| `@workspace/validation`        | Shared Zod schemas, domain validators                      |
| `@workspace/ui`                | shadcn/Radix components, Tailwind globals (web)            |
| `@workspace/jobs`              | BullMQ queue/job name constants, payload type contracts    |
| `@workspace/etl-core`          | Convex→Nest survey ETL pure transform logic                |
| `@workspace/excel-reports`     | ExcelJS workbook builders/parsers                          |
| `@workspace/audit-etl`         | Convex auditLogs→Postgres ETL                              |
| `@workspace/typescript-config` | Shared TSConfigs                                           |
| `@workspace/eslint-config`     | Shared ESLint configs                                      |

## Ownership boundaries

- **web** — UI, client state, browser. Never imports Prisma, NestJS, or server secrets.
- **api** — HTTP endpoints, business logic, Prisma, auth guards, job enqueuing. Never imports React/Next.js/RN.
- **worker** — job processing. HTTP is ops-only (`/live`, `/ready`, `/metrics`). Never imports API controllers.
- **mobile** — Expo/RN client. Never imports Next.js, DOM APIs, Prisma, NestJS, or server secrets.
- **api portal** — `v1/portal/*` for external ULB integrations (API-key auth, not Clerk JWT).
- **packages** — domain-independent reusables. Never import from `apps/*`.

## Dependency direction

```
apps/web    ──→ @workspace/ui, @workspace/validation
apps/api    ──→ @workspace/database, @workspace/validation, @workspace/jobs, @workspace/etl-core, @workspace/excel-reports
apps/worker ──→ @workspace/database, @workspace/jobs, @workspace/etl-core, @workspace/excel-reports, @workspace/audit-etl
apps/mobile ──→ @workspace/validation (and other RN-safe shared packages as justified)
```

Circular dependencies between apps or packages are forbidden.

## Rule priority (conflicts)

1. Security — never weaken auth, secrets, input validation
2. Data integrity — migrations, transactions, constraints
3. Architecture boundaries — ownership, dependency direction
4. API contracts — DTOs, envelope format, error codes
5. Technology-specific — NestJS, Next.js, Expo patterns
6. Testing
7. Code style

## Anti-patterns

- Do not create packages for one-off utilities; colocate with the app.
- Do not add repository/DDD layers beyond existing controller → service → repository.
- Do not import `apps/api` into `apps/worker` (or vice versa); share via packages.
- Do not import Next.js/DOM/browser-only libraries into `apps/mobile`.
- Do not put web UI (`@workspace/ui` Radix/DOM) into mobile unless a true RN-safe shared package exists.
